  "description": "Positioned within a secure, well-maintained complex in the heart of Como's most sought-after pocket, this two-bedroom, one-bathroom apartment delivers the kind of lifestyle that most renters spend months looking for and rarely find all in one place.<br/><br/>Inside, the apartment is comfortable, practical, and immediately liveable. The open-plan living and dining area is light-filled and easy to settle into, flowing out to a private balcony where the outlook reminds you exactly how well-located you are. The kitchen is functional and well-appointed, gas cooking, ample storage, and everything where you'd expect it to be. Both bedrooms are generously sized with built-in robes, serviced by a clean and well-presented bathroom. Split-system air conditioning keeps things comfortable year-round, and a secure car bay means the practicalities are well covered.<br/><br/>The complex is quiet and secure, the kind of building where people take pride in where they live, and it shows in every shared space.<br/><br/>The foreshore is metres from your front door, and weekend afternoons by the water are simply part of the routine here. The Preston Street café strip is a short flat stroll away, with some of Perth's best coffee, dining, and neighbourhood energy right at your disposal. Canning Bridge train station puts the CBD a quick ten minutes away by rail. Penrhos College, Como Secondary College, and Curtin University are all close by. The Swan River foreshore, Collier Park Golf Course, the South of Perth Yacht Club, and the Raffles Hotel round out a lifestyle that is genuinely hard to improve upon.<br/><br/>Melville Parade is one of Como's most tightly held streets and units in this complex move quickly when they come to market. This one is no different.<br/><br/>For more information on this property, please contact Noelia Stenvers today.<br/><br/>We look forward to welcoming you.",
